Here's a summary of TUnit's lifecycle hooks at each scope:

## 1. Before/After Every Test in a Class

```csharp
public class OrderTests
{
    [Before(Test)]
    public async Task ResetDatabase(TestContext context)
    {
        await InMemoryDb.ResetAsync();
    }

    [After(Test)]
    public async Task Cleanup(TestContext context)
    {
        // optional per-test teardown
    }

    [Test]
    public async Task Order_WithNoItems_Throws() { /* ... */ }
}
```

## 2. Once Before/After All Tests in a Class

```csharp
public class OrderTests
{
    [Before(Class)]
    public static async Task OpenFixture(ClassHookContext context)
    {
        // runs once before the first test in this class
    }

    [After(Class)]
    public static async Task DisposeFixture(ClassHookContext context)
    {
        // runs once after the last test in this class
    }

    [Test]
    public async Task PlaceOrder_Succeeds() { /* ... */ }
}
```

## 3. Once Before/After All Tests in the Assembly

```csharp
public class WireMockHook
{
    [Before(Assembly)]
    public static async Task StartServer(AssemblyHookContext context)
    {
        await WireMockServer.StartAsync();
    }

    [After(Assembly)]
    public static async Task StopServer(AssemblyHookContext context)
    {
        await WireMockServer.StopAsync();
    }
}
```

## 4. Once for the Entire Test Session (cross-assembly)

```csharp
public class GlobalDatabaseHook
{
    [Before(TestSession)]
    public static async Task ApplyMigrations(TestSessionContext context)
    {
        await EfCoreMigrator.MigrateAsync();
    }

    [After(TestSession)]
    public static async Task TearDownDatabase(TestSessionContext context)
    {
        await EfCoreMigrator.DropAsync();
    }
}
```

---

**Key points:**

| Scope | Attribute | Must be static? |
|-------|-----------|-----------------|
| Per-test | `[Before(Test)]` / `[After(Test)]` | No |
| Per-class | `[Before(Class)]` / `[After(Class)]` | **Yes** |
| Per-assembly | `[Before(Assembly)]` / `[After(Assembly)]` | **Yes** |
| Per-session | `[Before(TestSession)]` / `[After(TestSession)]` | **Yes** |

**Bonus:** Use `[BeforeEvery(Test)]` / `[AfterEvery(Test)]` (and `Class`/`Assembly` variants) on a standalone class to add *global* cross-cutting hooks that fire for every test everywhere—useful for logging or diagnostics without modifying each test class.
